{
  "id": 460054220,
  "iid": 23744,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ISAKMP: Add SHA1 verification to NAT_DETECTION_SOURCE_IP and NAT_DETECTION_DESTINATION_IP payloads",
  "description": "These payloads contain in notification_data field the SHA1 value described in RFC7296#2.3 and the verification of this particular value was implemented to know if NAT was detected or not.\n\n**NAT_DETECTION_SOURCE_IP** -\\> SHA(initiator_spi, responder_spi, source_ip, source_port)\n\n**NAT_DETECTION_DESTINATION_IP** -\\> SHA(initiator_spi, responder_spi, destination_ip, destination_port)\n\nHere you can see a picture how this verification is done:\n\n**NAT not detected (IPv4)**:\n\n![good_case_ipv4.png](/uploads/51df156d3f44b296187a9176a6d16da1/good_case_ipv4.png){width=\"655\" height=\"304\"}\n\n**NAT Detected (IPv4)**:\n\n![nat_detected.png](/uploads/4359d61d17ef477171900a480683e350/nat_detected.png){width=\"657\" height=\"383\"}\n\n**NAT not detected (IPv6)**:\n\n![ipv6_nat_not_detected.png](/uploads/5be7f23a912e65669b2c08cf69eadcb0/ipv6_nat_not_detected.png){width=\"657\" height=\"415\"}",
